Z||000003||OcalaFiero||09-10-2001||04:05 PM||||As far as plans, I'm not sure yet. I'm torn between doing a rstoration to stock condition and "mild" mods. I probably will "upgrade" to one of the optional wheel styles (Hi-tech etc) and need to replace the seats or recover them. Other than that it just has the the normal niggling problems (now that it runs again). The only problems/needs (that I know of) are Headlight motors, some minor wiring "fixes" that were done by the prvious owner and a new paint job. If I go the modified route, I'll probably try to find a GT Fascia and spoiler, but that's about it. The Wife has ruled out A V8 swap, but maybe I'll find a way to sneak it in.....<P>Mike<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR>'86 2M4<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||09-10-2001||04:28 PM||||It sure looks like its in good shape!  What kind of milage do you have on it?<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000005||OcalaFiero||09-10-2001||04:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>It sure looks like its in good shape!  What kind of milage do you have on it?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's got 49,500 miles on it. The Car sat up on and off for the last 10 years, (the previous owner was in the Navy). When I got it the front calipers wer locked up and there were a few electrical gremlins and other problems that crop up on a car that's seen little use. For the past month or so, after moving from Cleveland, Ohio to Florida, it's given me nothing but greif. I've replaced the fuel pump, rebuilt the throttle body, replaced most of the ignition system and rebult the exhaust from the cat on back to the tailpipe. She is running again and pretty smoothly at that. The paint on the roof and reardecklid is kind of hazy, and there are some chips in the hood, but I'll just have it repainted early next year.<P>Mike<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR>'86 2M4<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tonker||09-10-2001||10:20 PM||||Has it had all the recall stuff done on it? I notice you have weather stripping at the front( passenger compartment) end of your trunk. Mine was apparently removed during one of the recall  sessions.<P>She looks nice though!||||reg||14
